        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 1, name: "Home", item: "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/" },
        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 2, name: "By Price", item: "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/price/" },
        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 3, name: "Treadmills at Dick’s", item: "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/dicks-sporting-goods-treadmills/" },
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      mainEntity: [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Can you try treadmills at Dick’s Sporting Goods?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "In most stores, yes, and it is the main reason to go. Selection varies by store format — larger experiential formats set several machines up running, while a standard store may have three or four. Ring ahead and ask what is set up and powered on before making the trip, and take the shoes you will actually train in.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Are treadmills cheaper at Dick’s?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Competitive rather than reliably cheapest. The more useful lever is price matching, which retailers of this type commonly offer against named competitors — ask at the service desk for the specific item, since terms and exclusions vary. Bigger still is timing: seasonal discounting moves prices further than the spread between retailers does.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Is the Dick’s model the same as the one I read a review of?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Not necessarily. Large retailers frequently carry model variants with their own model numbers, and differences can reach the console, deck, motor rating or warranty. Write down the full designation including any suffix, find it on the manufacturer's site, and compare deck dimensions, continuous-duty motor rating, capacity and warranty terms.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Does Dick’s deliver and assemble treadmills?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "It depends on the item and the arrangement, so ask before buying rather than after. Large-item delivery ranges from kerbside to room-of-choice with assembly and packaging removal, and those are very different services. A boxed treadmill has no good handholds and will not fit in most cars, so plan delivery rather than collection.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Is an extended protection plan on a treadmill worth it?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "It depends entirely on what the manufacturer already provides. Some brands cover frame and motor for life with one to three years on parts and labour, and a plan that duplicates that is money for nothing. Ask what the factory warranty covers, whether the plan starts immediately or afterwards, and whether it includes labour and call-out — usually half the cost of any real repair.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Who repairs a treadmill bought at Dick’s?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "The manufacturer, not the retailer. The factory warranty covers the machine and the manufacturer's service network handles it, which makes the brand's parts availability more important than the shop's reputation — the shop is not who fixes it in year three. Photograph the serial plate on the frame and keep it with the receipt.",
          },
        },
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "Article",
      headline: title,
      description: description,
      author: { "@type": "Person", name: "Morgan Reyes" },
      datePublished: "2026-09-18",
      dateModified: "2026-09-18",
      publisher: { "@type": "Organization", name: "Treadmill Reviews USA" },
    },
  ],
};
