        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            The reason to go is the floor. <strong class="text-white">Four deliberate minutes on a
            running machine tells you whether the deck is long enough for your stride</strong> —
            the single specification that decides most treadmill satisfaction, and the one no
            listing can communicate.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Then do the model-number check before you pay, because retailer variants differ and the
            warranty is usually where it shows. And compare against
            <a href="/costco-treadmill/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">the warehouse route</a>
            and <a href="/best-time-of-year-to-buy-a-treadmill/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">the calendar</a>
            — timing moves the price further than the shop does.
          </p>
